e signal.", "whatIsNew": "Source authors’ specific experimental advance as summarized in the inspected sections; independent novelty certification not performed.", "limitations": "The initially guessed arXiv2404.02939 was a different paper and is retained privately as an identity mismatch; no inference uses it. Experimental methods and full uncertainty not independently reviewed.", "status": "abstract-only", "equationsUsed": ["freq-photon", "freq-comb"], "replication": "No laboratory reproduction, raw-data reanalysis or independent uncertainty-budget reconstruction performed.", "nextQuestions": ["Which systematic shifts and correlations limit the claimed observable?", "What external replication or independently reproducible data would test this result?"], "title": "Laser Excitation of the Th-229 Nucleus", "kind": "paper", "domain": "frequency"}</data></node><node id="freq-question-identifiability"><data key="title">Which calibrated extra channel or intervention separates source dynamics from transfer and sensor response?</data><data key="kind">question</data><data key="domain">frequency</data><data key="status">open-within-declared-model</data><data key="metadata">{"id": "freq-question-identifiability", "question": "Which calibrated extra channel or intervention separates source dynamics from transfer and sensor response?", "status": "open-within-declared-model", "neededEvidence": "Independent source excitation or transfer calibration; uncertainty, bandwidth, noise and explicit alternative models.", "sourceIds": ["freq-scipy-csd"], "title": "Which calibrated extra channel or intervention separates source dynamics from transfer and sensor response?", "kind": "question", "domain": "frequency"}</data></node><node id="freq-question-clock"><data key="title">Which uncertainties and systematic shifts limit a solid-state nuclear clock beyond a successful transition lock?</data><data key="kind">question</data><data key="domain">frequency</data><data key="status">selected-res